PATCH 229: reconstruct FUN_1000_66cd (asm 0x166cd = 0f69:0x703d) -- the object model-name copy's dropped
ES=STRSEG source base.  Asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0x166cd-0x166f1.

Called by 502f (patch 228) with si = the object's STRSEG name offset.  66cd copies the NUL-terminated name
from ES:[si] (ES = word[DGROUP:0x70] = STRSEG) into the render name buffer DGROUP:0x7a52 and sets
word[0x7a50]=0x168 / byte[0x87c2]=3.  Ghidra dropped the ES=STRSEG segment base (`*param_1` host-deref of
the raw si -> SIGSEGV); rebased src = g_mem + (STRSEG<<4) + si, dst through g_mem+0x1c000.

Cascade-only => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows.  Default boot rc=0, mainmenu unchanged.  Sources
pristine; fist.c via build/.
